Anointing

The Lord has taken His anointing oil (His Spirit), and
poured it upon my head. He has anointed me.
(Ex. 29:7 KJV Paraphrased).

The Lord has taken oil and has anointed me in the
midst of the people. The Spirit of the Lord is upon me
everyday forever. (1 Sam. 16:13 KJV paraphrased).

I am the Lord’s anointed, I cannot be harmed. I am His
prophet, I cannot be hurt
(1 Chron. 16:22, Ps 105: 15 KJV).

I enjoy a furnished table even in the presence of my
enemies. My head is anointed with oil; my cup runs
over. (Ps. 23:5 NKJV).

The Lord is my strength. He is my saving strength
because I am anointed. (Ps. 28:8 NKJV).
